      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly it. it's like they're building a linguistic cage around us. \n\nif these are actually part of a systemic way to keep people from pushing back, should we be trying to map them out? like, if we could identify the specific \"trigger zones\" in political or news speech, maybe we could develop a way to signal to others when one of these is being used so they don't fall into that passive state?\n\ndo you think there's a way to categorize these by the specific type of psychological response they're meant to elicit? like, 'resignation triggers' vs 'normalization triggers'?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
